WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.950
I grabbed hold, digging in my claws
te ni totte tsume o tateta

3
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.380
but the future
sono mirai wa

4
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:34.600
blurred together, colors running
nijimu iro ni kasunde mieta

5
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:41.200
A red that can swallow even summer's hues
natsu no iro mo nuritsubusu you na aka ni

6
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:47.920
bokura no koe kakikesareteiku you de
now attempts to blot out our voices

7
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.660
Move those halting feet of yours
tachidomaru sono ashi o fumidasou ze

8
00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:01.300
Don't let stand the lies for show
misekake no uso yarisugosu yori

9
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:07.550
I'll give up countless mornings for my vows
nandome no asa chikai to hikikaeru yo

10
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:16.100
For the dream that we shared
bokura ga miteita yume

11
00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:36.200
<b>Come In, World</b>

12
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.760
Oimo! Kashii!

13
00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:46.370
<b>Brogy the Red Ogre
Captain of the Giant Pirate Crew</b>

14
00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.230
Get rid of those annoying ships!

15
00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:51.190
Lead the soldiers to the right and left
and destroy the ships!

16
00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:51.340
<b>Dorry the Blue Ogre
Captain of the Giant Pirate Crew</b>

17
00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.900
Watch out for the cannonballs!

18
00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:58.240
Got it, Captains!

19
00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.380
<b>Kashii, Giant Pirate Crew</b>

20
00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:01.950
Let's go, guys!

21
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.100
<b>Oimo, Giant Pirate Crew</b>

22
00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:09.120
Where were they?!

23
00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.840
The legendary Giant Pirate Crew itself has arrived!

24
00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.340
We've confirmed the notorious Brogy the Red
and Dorry the Blue leading the crew!

25
00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:27.350
Why would all these warriors
from back then be here on this island?!

26
00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:30.940
The Giant Pirate Crew made landfall!

27
00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:33.570
Shoot at and repel those damn Giants!

28
00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.320
Go for it, boys!

29
00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.490
We'll go ahead!

30
00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:45.910
M...

31
00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.660
Masters!

32
00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.920
Why are they here?!

33
00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.830
Master Brogy!

34
00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.540
Master Dorry!

35
00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:57.090
Even Oimo and Kashii are here!

36
00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.800
I wonder if they brought those two
back from Little Garden.

37
00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:03.390
Oimo! Kashii!

38
00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.470
Yeah!

39
00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:10.350
Even if we went to Elbaph,
I thought we wouldn't be able to see them!

40
00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:16.520
A long time ago,
the world feared the Giant Pirate Crew,

41
00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:20.240
but they disbanded due to a huge quarrel
between their two Captains, Dorry and Brogy.

42
00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:25.450
Luffy and the others
stumbled into their century-long feud.

43
00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.080
And on a different island,
they met Oimo and Kashii...

44
00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.210
...who went to see
how their bosses were doing

45
00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.580
and became friends.

46
00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:38.880
They're clearly attacking the Marine ships!

47
00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:40.800
I can't believe they are your friends!

48
00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:43.890
They must've found out about this
and hurried here!

49
00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.470
What? How?

50
00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.970
This incident is a Government-related attack.

51
00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:50.100
It'd be in the news by the next day.

52
00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.440
Though I'm sure
they're reporting the Government favorably.

53
00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:54.270
So this is a major story!

54
00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:56.440
Yeah, it must be!

55
00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.530
The masters didn't come here for war!

56
00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:05.370
They came to help us escape!

57
00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.120
Hurry up and get ready to go!

58
00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.540
Brook, where are you now?

59
00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:15.460
Why do I hear a scream?

60
00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:19.750
Don't worry!
I'll be there soon with the Sunny!

61
00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:20.630
You're the best!

62
00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:24.090
Yeah, we'll be passing through in a moment.

63
00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:24.800
Stop the ship!

64
00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:25.720
Ouch!

65
00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.930
If we fall off the island,
we'll hit the barrier and explode!

66
00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.640
Hello? It's me, Lilith!

67
00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:36.060
Listen, this bonehead
didn't think twice and...

68
00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:47.200
It's quite an uproar.

69
00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.950
We must at least be prepared
to escape any minute!

70
00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.290
It's not the time to be fighting, Zoro.

71
00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:59.710
You're so persistent! I'm in a hurry!

72
00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:06.010
Only the one
who'll win at the end can say that.

73
00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:07.550
Roronoa!

74
00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:16.850
Besides, right now you’re the pain in the ass
for making your friends wait!

75
00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.690
I’m not wrong, am I?

76
00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:26.740
You guys are a bunch of idiots
who can't leave a single one of your crew behind.

77
00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.700
As long as you're breathing,

78
00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.660
your crewmates are trapped here.

79
00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.200
You say that...

80
00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:39.290
...as if you're in control of
how long we fight.

81
00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.840
Rob Lucci!

82
00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.090
What's the damage report on our ships?

83
00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:54.390
About 30 small and medium vessels
have sunk!

84
00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.310
And the numbers are rising!

85
00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:00.770
Small and medium vessels, fall back!
Only warships, move forward!

86
00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:02.190
We're getting nowhere like this!

87
00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:04.730
Yes, Vice Admiral Red King!

88
00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:10.910
Why do we have to attack our own weapons?!

89
00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.550
Hey, Bonney!

90
00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:28.090
Why are you crying?

91
00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:32.260
Of course I'm crying, you idiot...

92
00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:35.430
I've been looking for you!

93
00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:39.690
I've been with you all this time!

94
00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:43.400
But I didn't know that you were Nika!

95
00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:45.860
Nika? What's that?

96
00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.190
I've always been...

97
00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:53.700
...wanting to throw
a rubber punch like you!

98
00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:57.580
I remember seeing your weak little punch.

99
00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:00.160
Then show me the real one!

100
00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.000
Punch him...

101
00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:05.460
...for Vegapunk!

102
00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.510
What?! Vegapunk!

103
00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:16.850
You foolish insects.

104
00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:20.850
There is a reason you deserve to die.

105
00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:22.850
No, there isn't.

106
00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:29.610
Get us off the island!

107
00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.740
All right, Bonney!

108
00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:35.280
Let's do it!

109
00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:37.790
And from now on,

110
00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.330
throw a punch like this!

111
00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:57.180
How could you hurt my friend?!

112
00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.560
Gum-Gum...

113
00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:04.850
...Dawn...

114
00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.810
...Gatling!

115
00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:42.100
We gotta get away on our own!

116
00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:43.140
Come on, Bonney!

117
00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:47.980
Use the hover function!
It allows you to fly low over the island.

118
00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:52.070
Vegapunk! Come with us!

119
00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:57.110
You go on ahead, Bonney...

120
00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:01.580
I know quite a lot about medical science.

121
00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:03.540
If I...

122
00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:05.920
...move now,

123
00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.210
I'll die.

124
00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:09.710
What?!

125
00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:12.920
You'll die even if you don't move.

126
00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.470
Give up.

127
00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:37.030
You've got to be kidding!
That was a laser beam!

128
00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:42.950
Love is stronger than light!

129
00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:45.620
If that were true,

130
00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:49.670
physics as we know it would be dead.

131
00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:52.130
All right, let's go!

132
00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:56.720
It's the northeast coast, right?!

133
00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:57.380
Yeah!

134
00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:08.520
I'll lose face...

135
00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:14.440
...if I don't at least
bring back your heads...

136
00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.490
Just write a letter of apology.

137
00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:38.590
My, my.
How the Five Elders have fallen.

138
00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:47.560
I wonder what kind of power this is...

139
00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:56.360
I've never heard of the Five Elders
personally descending to the lower world.

140
00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:01.360
But it’s helped us quite a bit.

141
00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:04.450
Okay, mission complete.

142
00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:08.290
Why are you two here?

143
00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:13.130
<b>Catarina Devon, Captain of the Sixth Ship
Blackbeard Pirates (Dog-Dog Fruit,
Mythical Type, Model: Nine-Tailed Fox)</b>

144
00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:15.590
<b>Van Augur, Captain of the Third Ship
Blackbeard Pirates (Warp-Warp Fruit)</b>

145
00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.710
Catarina Devon...

146
00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:24.010
I never thought the savages from Level 6
would submit to someone.

147
00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:26.600
Teach is special.

148
00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:28.680
As is his bloodline.

149
00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:31.190
Oh, you were aware of that?

150
00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:38.980
You people are always making strange moves.
What are you really after?

151
00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:42.450
The world.

152
00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:04.840
All right. Let's go back.

153
00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:06.760
We're still on the island.

154
00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:10.270
Couldn't you warp us a little farther?

155
00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:12.640
I'm still under training.

156
00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:17.400
W...! W...!

157
00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:24.780
W... Wait!

158
00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:26.410
Please wait!

159
00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:30.540
I didn't expect to see you here!

160
00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:33.750
"Supersonic" Van Augur!

161
00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:36.960
"The Crescent Moon Hunter" Catarina Devon!

162
00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:39.250
I'm Caribou!

163
00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:41.420
I'm a pirate! If I may be so bold!

164
00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:45.090
I've been looking for you folks!

165
00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:49.640
I set out to sea wishing to be like him!

166
00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:55.020
My dream is to become
one of "Blackbeard" Teach-sama's men!

167
00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:56.900
Please, I beg you!

168
00:12:56.980 --> 00:13:01.860
Let me see him for a moment!

169
00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:04.360
What?!

170
00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:09.160
Wait, wait! Please wait!

171
00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:11.870
Who is this guy?

172
00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:13.620
Wet-Haired Caribou...

173
00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:17.370
That's right!
Just hold your fire, please!

174
00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:21.500
He is a pirate,
but this is a Government island.

175
00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:25.630
The commodore has many assassins after him.

176
00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:29.140
I'm absolutely not one of them!
Believe me!

177
00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:34.350
If you guys kill me now,
Teach-sama will bash your heads in!

178
00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:36.640
Oh... Why?

179
00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:42.820
B-Because I've got information
that no one else has!

180
00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:50.030
They're the Ancient Weapons named after gods
that existed a long time ago.

181
00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:52.790
One of them, Poseidon,

182
00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:56.870
refers to the power of
Princess Shirahoshi of Fish-Man Island.

183
00:13:57.160 --> 00:14:02.380
And another one, Pluton,
lies beneath the Land of Wano.

184
00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:08.130
The terrifying Ancient Weapons are
said to have the power to destroy the world.

185
00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:10.590
The Straw Hats and I are probably...

186
00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:15.180
...the only ones in this world
who know where the two of them are.

187
00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:20.730
If you let me meet Teach-sama,

188
00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:23.440
I'll give you all the information I have!

189
00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:25.900
I'm sure it'll make him happy!

190
00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:27.860
So please take me to him!

191
00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:30.740
I'll definitely be useful to you!

192
00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:36.700
All ships! Get away from the coast!

193
00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:36.850
<b>Vice Admiral Doberman</b>

194
00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:39.420
Don't fight the Pacifistas!

195
00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:46.670
Damn! The Bubble Shield again!

196
00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:51.840
Why do we have to be reminded of
the power of the Special Science Group?!

197
00:14:59.310 --> 00:15:01.980
Fighting them doesn't excite us!

198
00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:05.610
A win is a loss, and a loss is an injustice!

199
00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:05.610
<b>Vice Admiral Bluegrass</b>

200
00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:09.150
The Giants made landfall
on the other side of the island!

201
00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:12.180
<b>Vice Admiral Urban</b>

202
00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:12.030
A series of unexpected events is happening!

203
00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:16.740
Could the Buster Call be called off?
That would be unprecedented.

204
00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:16.890
<b>Vice Admiral Hound</b>

205
00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:23.610
<b>Vice Admiral Guillotine</b>

206
00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:21.650
Vegapunk was the one who gave a pirate power over the Pacifistas!

207
00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.460
Calling it off is not an option!

208
00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:28.420
He's a complete traitor to the Government!
A major offender!

209
00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:33.590
To turn things around,
we need to take back the Pacifistas!

210
00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:37.850
Take out the pirate Jewelry Bonney!

211
00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:42.390
Vice admirals! Leave your position
and eliminate Jewelry Bonney!

212
00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:45.860
She's currently moving away
from the center of the Fabriophase...

213
00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:48.360
...to the northeast coast!

214
00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:49.570
I repeat!

215
00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:52.450
Eliminate Jewelry Bonney!

216
00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:55.450
Got it!

217
00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:57.910
This is Tosa. Target confirmed!

218
00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:58.060
<b>Marine HQ
Vice Admiral Tosa</b>

219
00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:00.660
I'll get close and execute the order!

220
00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:08.050
These claws are ten Finger Pistols
that will even shred armor!

221
00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:09.250
What?!

222
00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:12.970
Tosa Bite!

223
00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:32.320
What?!
Why are the Giants here on this island?!

224
00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:35.360
We're in a hurry,
but now we have more enemies?!

225
00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:39.200
Who are you guys?

226
00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:43.160
I researched the new members
on their wanted posters,

227
00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:45.290
but I don't recognize any of you.

228
00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.460
Are you lab workers from this island?

229
00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:51.130
We're here for the Straw Hats!

230
00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:55.880
Luffy is our captain...
What do you have against him?!

231
00:16:56.010 --> 00:17:00.220
No, we have nothing against him,
just gratitude!

232
00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:02.850
We're Elbaph warriors!

233
00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:06.100
If you're their friends,
we'll protect you at all costs!

234
00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:13.900
Come on! You scared me!

235
00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:17.030
Our bad, sorry!

236
00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:25.250
Luffy, Sanji, and Vegapunk
are still at the center of the island!

237
00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:26.420
Will you help them?!

238
00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:29.000
Those names bring back memories!

239
00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:31.210
Of course we will!

240
00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:32.710
Thanks!

241
00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:37.380
Vegapunk is supposed to be the man
that scholar was talking about.

242
00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:38.800
Yeah.

243
00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:42.720
Take them to the ship!

244
00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:44.180
Will do!

245
00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:58.240
Let's hurry on!

246
00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:00.570
The fire has spread quite a bit!

247
00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:02.700
Okay, Bosses!

248
00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:06.910
Leave everything to those two.
You don't have to worry about a thing.

249
00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:12.340
Are they the ones that
Usopp calls his masters all the time?

250
00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:21.180
Tosa's communication is cut off.

251
00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.430
He got beaten in a counterattack?

252
00:18:23.470 --> 00:18:25.220
Or he ran into a Giant?

253
00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:27.500
<b>Vice Admiral Pomsky</b>

254
00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:27.420
I'm going onto the island!

255
00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:32.310
I'll attack from the sea!

256
00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:41.990
Hop on, Doll!

257
00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.660
There is an Elbaph ship
on the northeast coast.

258
00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:51.290
The strength of the Giants varies greatly.
Have you ever fought them?

259
00:18:52.210 --> 00:18:55.750
More than two decades ago,
I had a Giant as a boss.

260
00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:57.710
“Had”...?

261
00:18:57.760 --> 00:18:58.760
You mean Saul?

262
00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:01.050
He was a strong one.

263
00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:06.430
Where are the rest of your crew members?

264
00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:10.020
They're at a lab above the clouds.

265
00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:12.400
Above the clouds? Is it a Sky Island?

266
00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:13.690
No.

267
00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:15.520
It's right there.

268
00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:17.820
That's the one.

269
00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:30.040
You're not gonna make it
if you don't beat it!

270
00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:31.290
Ow, ow, ow!

271
00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.330
I'll bleed if I move!

272
00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:51.060
Old Man Apple!

273
00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:55.730
We promised you
we'd help you escape from the island!

274
00:19:56.480 --> 00:20:00.190
I know I asked for that, but...

275
00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:03.450
...now I’ve made up my mind!

276
00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:07.530
There is something here that I must protect.

277
00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:12.250
I wanted to tell Bonney...

278
00:20:12.460 --> 00:20:16.540
...about her authority
when she was a little older...

279
00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:21.170
Her life is inevitably in danger...

280
00:20:21.510 --> 00:20:23.800
Please keep her safe...

281
00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:30.720
You look much less human now.

282
00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:33.100
You've got an insane look in your eyes.

283
00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:39.020
Are you coated with poison or something?

284
00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:42.740
Look out, Luffy!

285
00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:52.750
Sanji!

286
00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:54.920
Get the old man outta here!

287
00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:57.170
Don't worry if it hurts to move him!

288
00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:58.630
Okay!

289
00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:07.260
Come on! Come on!

290
00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:12.890
Ow, ow, ow...

291
00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:15.770
Hey! That's enough, Sanji!

292
00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:17.400
Just be still!

293
00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:31.830
What?!

294
00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:32.700
No!

295
00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:51.560
Vegapunk!

296
00:21:52.930 --> 00:21:54.100
Old Man Apple!

297
00:21:59.310 --> 00:22:01.190
Sanji! Run!

298
00:22:01.230 --> 00:22:02.820
To the back of the island!

299
00:22:12.740 --> 00:22:13.660
Dammit!

300
00:22:14.450 --> 00:22:16.620
I'm sorry, Vegapunk!

301
00:22:27.630 --> 00:22:29.760
You bastards...

302
00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:42.190
...aren't going anywhere!

303
00:22:56.410 --> 00:22:58.290
What's wrong, Vegapunk?

304
00:22:58.330 --> 00:22:59.660
Stay with me!

305
00:23:00.250 --> 00:23:01.460
Dammit!

306
00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:03.170
Hey! Vegapunk!

307
00:23:03.460 --> 00:23:04.590
Are you dead?!

308
00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:07.960
Hey! Why are you smiling?!

309
00:23:21.640 --> 00:23:24.270
Um... Hello?

310
00:23:24.310 --> 00:23:25.520
Check, check.

311
00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:30.240
Come in! Come in, world!

312
00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:35.030
I'm Dr. Vegapunk.

313
00:23:35.200 --> 00:23:37.830
I'm a humble genius scientist.

314
00:23:38.080 --> 00:23:42.080
The message I'm about to leave
will likely shock everyone,

315
00:23:42.670 --> 00:23:44.420
but it is...

316
00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:47.420
...the truth of this world!

317
